statistics: [...] = robustcov (..., name, value)
Robust multivariate covariance and mean estimate.

sig = robustcov (X) returns a robust estimate sig of
the covariance matrix of the NxP data matrix X, computed so that
it is not distorted by outlying observations. Rows of X are
observations and columns are variables. Rows containing NaN values
are removed with a warning.

[sig, mu, mah, outliers, s] = robustcov
(...) also returns the robust mean mu (1xP), the robust
Mahalanobis distances mah (Nx1) of each observation from the
estimated distribution, a logical vector outliers (Nx1) flagging
observations whose distance exceeds sqrt (chi2inv (0.975, P)),
and a structure s holding the estimate metadata. mah and
outliers have one row per row of X; for removed rows, mah
is NaN and outliers is false. When sig is not
positive definite, every distance is 0, removed rows included, and no
observation is flagged.

Additional parameters can be specified by Name-Value pair arguments.

Name Value
'Method' the estimator, one of 'fmcd' (default,
the Fast Minimum Covariance Determinant algorithm), 'ogk' (the
Orthogonalized Gnanadesikan-Kettenring estimator) or
'olivehawkins' (the Olive-Hawkins concentration algorithm). If any
of 'ReweightingMethod', 'StartMethod' or
'NumConcentrationSteps' is given and 'Method' is not, the
method is 'olivehawkins'.
'OutlierFraction' the maximum fraction of outliers, a
scalar in [0, 0.5] (default 0.5), used to set the size of the
subsets in 'fmcd' and 'olivehawkins'. It is not valid for
'ogk'.
'NumTrials' a positive integer. For 'fmcd' it is
the number of random elemental subsets drawn (default 500). For
'olivehawkins' it is the number of starts and must equal the number
of starts in 'StartMethod' (default 2); with 'elemental'
alone it is the number of random starts. It is not valid for
'ogk'.
'BiasCorrection' a logical scalar (default true)
that applies the small-sample bias correction to the raw and the reweighted
'fmcd' estimate. Only valid for 'fmcd'.
'NumOGKIterations' the number of orthogonalization
iterations for 'ogk', a positive integer (default 2). Only valid
for 'ogk'.
'UnivariateEstimator' the robust univariate
location/scale estimator used by 'ogk', either 'tauscale'
(default) or 'qn'. Only valid for 'ogk'.
'ReweightingMethod' the reweighting used by
'olivehawkins', either 'rfch' (default) or 'rmvn'.
'NumConcentrationSteps' the number of concentration
steps taken from each start by 'olivehawkins', a positive integer
(default 10).
'StartMethod' the starts of 'olivehawkins': one of
'classical', 'medianball' or 'elemental', a function
handle [T, C] = f (X) returning a 1xP location and a
PxP scatter, or a cell array of these. The default is
{'classical', 'medianball'}.

Note on reproducibility. 'fmcd' and the 'elemental'
start of 'olivehawkins' draw random subsets, so their exact estimate
depends on the random number generator and is not identical to
MATLAB's on data where the optimal subset is ambiguous; on well-separated
data both converge to the same estimate.

Small-sample correction. With 'BiasCorrection' enabled,
'fmcd' scales the raw and the reweighted covariance by the
small-sample factors of Pison, Van Aelst and Willems (2002), interpolated
over 1 - OutlierFraction, as the covMcd function of the
R package robustbase computes them. Where those formulas give negative or
very large factors, at the default 'OutlierFraction' for up to 9
variables and small samples, the simulated factors of robustbase are used
instead. MATLAB applies the formulas there as well, so it can return a
covariance with negative variances (for example, with 3 variables and 6 to
8 observations), and for 2 variables it uses other factors, so its estimate
differs from this one at every sample size. When the subset is the whole
sample, the classical estimate is reweighted with no small-sample factor.

Singular subsets. If 'olivehawkins' finds a singular
subset, a warning is issued and the selected estimate is returned without
reweighting. A singular estimate gives zero robust distances. When
several starts end in singular subsets, the 'medianball' start is
selected if present, otherwise the first one listed in 'StartMethod'.

